# Cambodia public holiday API - refresh schedule
#
# Install with:  crontab deploy/crontab.example
# Adjust APP_DIR to wherever you deployed the binaries.

SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
APP_DIR=/opt/khmer-holiday-api
KHAPI_DB=/opt/khmer-holiday-api/data/holidays.db
TZ=Asia/Phnom_Penh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Watch for NEXT year's sub-decree.
#
# The Royal Government signs the holiday sub-decree around September of the
# preceding year (2026's was signed 5 September 2025 and published as Prakas
# No. 216/25 on 18 September 2025). Checking weekly from July onward catches it
# within days of publication without hammering the ministry sites year-round.
#
# Every Monday 06:00, July through December.
0 6 * 7-12 1  cd $APP_DIR && ./bin/khapi-scrape scrape -year $(date +\%Y -d '+1 year') >> logs/scrape.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Re-verify the CURRENT year monthly.
#
# Catches the rare mid-year amendment - a holiday moved for a state funeral or
# a substitute day added when a holiday falls on a weekend.
#
# 1st of each month, 06:30.
30 6 1 * *    cd $APP_DIR && ./bin/khapi-scrape scrape -year $(date +\%Y) >> logs/scrape.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Early-January rollover.
#
# On 2 January, pull the new current year and the following year so the API is
# never left serving only stale data.
0 7 2 1 *     cd $APP_DIR && ./bin/khapi-scrape scrape >> logs/scrape.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE ON dates BSD vs GNU
#
# `date -d` above is GNU coreutils (Linux). On macOS/BSD use instead:
#   $(date -v+1y +%Y)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AFTER THE SUB-DECREE IS PUBLISHED
#
# The scraper marks dates "reported" once the announced day count matches what
# it holds. Promoting to "official" is a deliberate human step, because the
# governing Prakas is a scanned PDF that no scraper can read:
#
#   ./bin/khapi-scrape status                  # see which years are provisional
#   ./bin/khapi-scrape scrape -year 2027       # note the Prakas PDF URL it found
#   # ... open the PDF, check the dates ...
#   ./bin/khapi-scrape verify -year 2027 \
#       -decree "Prakas No. NNN/26" \
#       -url https://mlvt.gov.kh/media/k2/attachments/YYYYMMDD_NNN.pdf
#
# If the sub-decree moved a lunar date away from the projection, re-scrape that
# year with -replace first so the stale date is removed rather than orphaned:
#
#   ./bin/khapi-scrape scrape -year 2027 -replace
